{{Quote|Small, green, and wrinkly with pointy ears.|[[Ezra Bridger]] talking about [[Kanan Jarrus]]' description of Yoda|<ref name="Shroud">{{Rebels|Shroud of Darkness}}</ref>}}
The '''species''' to which the [[Jedi]] [[Grand Master]] [[Yoda]] belonged was ancient and shrouded in mystery. Members of this species were rarely seen anywhere in [[the galaxy]]. The few members of this species seen in the [[galaxy]] were all [[Force-sensitive]], and the species' [[Yoda's homeworld|homeworld]] and name were unknown.

==Biology and appearance==
{{Quote|Wait. They said fifty years old.''"<br />"''Species age differently. Perhaps it could live many centuries.|Din Djarin and IG-11 upon discovering an infant of the species|<ref name="Chapter 1" />}}
[[File:Grogu-SWI216.png|thumb|left|200px|Din Grogu, an infant member of the species.]]
The [[species]] included male<ref name="Databank YOD">{{Databank|yoda|Yoda}}</ref> and female [[gender]]s.<ref name="Databank YAD" /> Members of the species were small in size, roughly comparable to that of a [[human]] child, with [[Color|green]] skin, large [[eye]]s, and long pointed [[ear]]s. Their three-fingered hands ended in claws.<ref name="Revenge of the Sith" /> One member of the species, [[Din Grogu|Grogu]], caught and [[Diet|devoured]] live [[amphibian]]s whole,<ref name="The Reckoning" /> while another member, [[Yoda]], made [[rootleaf stew]]s.<ref name="CL2016" /> Their ears were expressive, curling, and unfurling in accordance with their emotions.<ref name="Dark Disciple" />

Members of the species were capable of growing thin [[hair]], with shades varying from auburn to white being documented, females having longer and thicker hair than males. The species had a very long life expectancy, spanning at least several [[Standard century|centuries]]; [[Yoda]] lived nearly a thousand years before dying of old age,<ref name="AEYNTK" /> and they aged very slowly, remaining in infancy for at least fifty [[standard year]]s.<ref name="Chapter 1" /> Even at this stage of life, certain [[Force-sensitive]] individuals of this species could use [[Force power]]s such as [[telekinesis]] and [[Force healing]];<ref name="The Reckoning" /><ref name="Chapter 2">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 2: The Child}}</ref> they were also capable of complex thought processes, and could understand speech and communicate via the Force at this age.<ref name="The Jedi">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 13: The Jedi}}</ref> Despite their slow aging for the first five [[Standard decade|decades]] of life,<ref name="Chapter 1" /> members of the species reached maturity by their hundredth year, as exemplified by the [[Jedi]] [[Yoda]], who began [[Jedi training|training]] other Jedi when he was about one hundred years old.<ref name="AEYNTK" /> According to [[Yaddle]], Yoda was considered to be middle-aged<ref name="Cataclysm">''[[The High Republic: Cataclysm]]''</ref> at 514.<ref name="Middle-aged">''[[The High Republic: Cataclysm]]'' features the [[Night of Sorrow]], which ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates to [[382 BBY]]. ''Timelines'' also states that [[Yoda]] was born in [[896 BBY]], meaning that he must have been 514 during the events of ''Cataclysm''.</ref>

==Society and culture==
{{Quote|I want to tell you about someone you remind me of a great deal. His name was Yoda. He was small like you, but his heart was huge and the Force was strong in him. He once said to me 'Size matters not.' That's how he talked. He would speak in riddles. Have you heard anyone talk like that back home?|Luke Skywalker to Grogu|<ref name="BOBF 6">{{BOBF|Chapter 6: From the Desert Comes a Stranger}}</ref>}}
Due to the rarity of the species in the wider [[The galaxy|galaxy]],<ref name="Complete Visual New" /> little was known about them except that the species was ancient and shrouded in mystery.<ref name="Card Trader">[[Star Wars: Card Trader|''Star Wars'': Card Trader]]</ref> Members of the species were capable of speaking [[Galactic Basic Standard]], although Yoda often used a distinctive syntax.<ref name="The Empire Strikes Back" />

==History==
===Yoda, Grand Master of the Jedi===
{{Quote|Do, or do not. There is no try.|Yoda to Luke Skywalker|audio=ThereIsNoTry-ESB.flac|<ref name="The Empire Strikes Back" />}}
[[File:Yoda_Episode_I_Canon.png|thumb|right|250px|Yoda served as Grand Master of the Jedi Order when he was almost nine centuries old.]]
Yoda, the last [[Grand Master]] of the [[Jedi Order]] prior to its [[Great Jedi Purge|fall]] at the end of the [[Clone Wars]],<ref name="Revenge of the Sith" /> was a member of the species born around the [[standard year]] [[896 BBY]].<ref name="Yoda Age">In [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode V ''Return of the Jedi'']], set in [[4 ABY]] by ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'', Yoda says he is 900 years old. Therefore, basic math indicates he must have been born around [[896 BBY]].</ref> He began training other Jedi when he was around a century old.<ref name="AEYNTK" /> Over the centuries, Yoda, who never revealed what [[Yoda's homeworld|his homeworld]] was,<ref name="Complete Visual New" /> trained many Jedi before eventually becoming the Grand Master of the entire order.<ref name="Revenge of the Sith" /> One of his final [[Padawan]]s was [[Dooku]], a [[human]] male who eventually left the Order and fell to the [[Dark side of the Force|dark side]], becoming the [[Sith Lord]] [[Darth]] Tyranus, who served as [[Darth Sidious]]' right-hand man in the orchestration of the Clone Wars.<ref name="DJL">''[[Dooku: Jedi Lost]]''</ref> When Sidious, publicly [[Supreme Chancellor]] Palpatine, revealed himself and issued [[Order 66]], which killed most Jedi across the galaxy, Yoda was one of the few survivors, returning to [[Coruscant]] and [[Duel in the Galactic Senate|dueling]] the self-declared [[Galactic Emperor]]; however, Yoda was forced to retreat.<ref name="Revenge of the Sith" /> Yoda subsequently went into hiding on the remote planet [[Dagobah]], eventually training one final student, [[Luke Skywalker]], during the [[Galactic Civil War]] to overthrow Sidious' [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="The Empire Strikes Back" /> Yoda died on Dagobah shortly before the [[Battle of Endor]], afterwards becoming a [[Force spirit]].<ref name="ROTJ">{{Film|VI}}</ref>

===Yaddle of the Jedi Council===
{{Quote|Yaddle is known for being very kind and quiet, but on the other hand possesses some of the deadliest Force powers.|An artist, in [[Unidentified artist's journal|his journal]]|<ref name="Alien Archive">''[[Star Wars: Alien Archive]]''</ref>}}
[[File:YaddleJediCouncil.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Yaddle served on the Jedi High Council at the same time as Yoda.]]
During the same period of time, one other member of the species, Yaddle, was also a member of the Jedi Order.<ref name="Databank YAD" /> Born in [[509 BBY]],<ref name="Yaddle Age">According to ''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]'', Yaddle was 477 [[Standard year|years]] old at the time of the [[invasion of Naboo]]. Since ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates that to [[32 BBY]], Yaddle was born in [[509 BBY]].</ref> she was a [[Jedi Master]] and member of the [[Jedi High Council]] during the [[Invasion of Naboo]].<ref name="The Phantom Menace">{{Film|I}}</ref> She trained multiple Padawans, among them [[Oppo Rancisis]]<ref name="Character Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> and [[Jaro Tapal]].<ref name="Jedi Survivor">''[[Star Wars Jedi: Survivor]]''</ref> After the [[Battle of Naboo]], Yaddle decided to take a less active role in Jedi affairs<ref name="USW">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref> and stepped down from the Council.<ref name="Databank YAD" /> Yaddle then pursued [[Count of Serenno]] and former Jedi Master [[Dooku]] after observing suspicious behavior on his part. She ended up [[Duel in the Works|encountering]] the [[Dark Lord of the Sith]] [[Darth Sidious]], who ordered the [[count]] to kill the Jedi. Yaddle was subsequently defeated and murdered by Dooku, another step on his path to the dark side.<ref name="The Sith Lord">{{TOTJ|The Sith Lord}}</ref>

===Din Grogu, the Mandalorian foundling===
{{Quote|He was raised at the Jedi Temple on Coruscant. Many Masters trained him over the years. At the end of the Clone Wars when the Empire rose to power, he was hidden. Someone took him from the Temple. Then his memory becomes dark. He seemed lost. Alone.|Ahsoka Tano feeling Grogu's thoughts|<ref name="The Jedi" />}}
Around [[41 BBY]],<ref name="Child Age">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 1: The Mandalorian}} indicates that [[Din Grogu|Grogu]] was 50 years old by the time of [[9 ABY]], which ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]'' takes place in. Using simple math, we can deduce that Grogu was born 41 years before the [[Battle of Yavin]], which was depicted in [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'' Episode IV ''A New Hope'']].</ref> Grogu was born. At some point before [[19 BBY]], he was raised at the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] on Coruscant, where many masters trained him over the years until the end of the Clone Wars when the Galactic Empire rose to power.<ref name="The Jedi" /> By [[9 ABY]], Grogu was kept in a [[Nikto hideout|compound]] on the planet [[Arvala-7]], guarded by a [[Unidentified Nikto mercenary gang|faction]] of [[Nikto]] [[Mercenary|mercenaries]] against various [[bounty hunter]]s sent after him. Eventually, [[Din Djarin]] and [[IG-11]] [[Mission to Arvala-7|defeated]] the mercenaries, with Djarin leaving with Grogu after destroying the [[assassin droid]], whose instructions had been to kill the infant while Djarin's had been to take him alive if possible.<ref name="Chapter 1" /> Although he initially handed Grogu over to his client, Djarin had a change of heart and chose to return and rescue him,<ref name="The Sin">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 3: The Sin}}</ref> placing both him and Grogu in the crosshairs of an [[Gideon's Imperial remnant|Imperial remnant]] headed by the war criminal [[Moff]] [[Gideon]], who wanted Grogu for his own purposes.<ref name="The Reckoning" /> After prevailing in an initial [[Clash on Nevarro|battle]] against Gideon's forces, Djarin, now acting as Grogu's father by [[Mandalorian Creed]], was charged with protecting Grogu until he could get him to either his own people or a Jedi.<ref name="Redemption">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 8: Redemption}}</ref>

[[File:Child-Mythosaur-TMS1C8.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Grogu was a foundling discovered by the Mandalorian bounty hunter Din Djarin.]]
After many adventures, Din Djarin finally found [[Ahsoka Tano]], a former Jedi [[Padawan]]. However, Ahsoka refused to train Grogu because of his feelings of anger, and fear, and his attachment to Djarin. Ahsoka then told Djarin to go to the ruins of an [[Force-henge|ancient temple]] on [[Tython]].<ref name="The Jedi" /> On Tython, Grogu reached out with the Force while members of Gideon's forces attempted to capture him. He was eventually [[Battle of Tython (9 ABY)|captured]] by Gideon's [[Phase-III Dark Trooper|Dark Troopers]], and brought aboard his [[Gideon's light cruiser|light cruiser]].<ref name="The Tragedy">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 14: The Tragedy}}</ref> He was later [[Second rescue of Grogu|rescued]] by Djarin and the timely intervention of Luke Skywalker.<ref name="The Rescue">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 16: The Rescue}}</ref>

==Yoda's species in the galaxy==
{{Quote|Is he your brother?''"<br />"''Hush, child. He is not. He is Master Yoda, a great teacher.|[[Cippa Tarko]], questioning Yaddle's relationship to Yoda.|<ref name="Cataclysm" />}}
The species, its origins shrouded in mystery,<ref name="Card Trader" /> was rarely seen, with only a few members known to the wider galaxy.<ref name="Complete Visual New" /> All known members of the species active in the galaxy were [[The Force|Force]] users and affiliated with the Jedi.<ref name="Databank YAD" /><ref name="Databank YOD" /><ref name="Chapter 2" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|So he's a mystery character. He's a magical character. He has no background. He comes and he goes. He's the subversive secret mysterious stranger that enters the film and then exits at the end.|George Lucas, about Yoda|<ref name="Unscripted">{{YouTube|video=Sk7RN3t2v14|text='Star Wars: Episode III - Revenge of the Sith' &#124; Unscripted &#124; Hayden Christensen, George Lucas|channel=@moviefone|name=Moviefone}}</ref>}}
''[[Star Wars]]'' creator [[George Lucas]] chose to keep the name and background of Yoda's species a mystery.<ref name="Unscripted" /> Both Yoda and [[Yaddle]]'s [[Databank (2014-)|Databank]] entries on [[StarWars.com]] list their species as "Unknown."<ref name="Databank YAD" /><ref name="Databank YOD" /> Interviewed for [[The Clone Wars: Season Three|''The Clone Wars'': Season Three]], Supervising Director [[Dave Filoni]] confirmed the show had no plans to reveal [[Yoda's homeworld]], further stating that he believed the world would never actually be seen in any story. To Filoni, giving such an answer would ruin a major part of the fun of Yoda's character: the mystery of his origins.<ref name="Third Wave">{{InsiderCite|120|Third Wave!}}</ref>

In the documentary "From Puppets to Pixels," available on the DVD bonus disc of [[Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones|''Star Wars'': Episode II ''Attack of the Clones'']], Lucas joked that Yoda was "the illegitimate child of [[Wikipedia:Kermit the Frog|Kermit the Frog]] and [[Wikipedia:Miss Piggy|Miss Piggy]]."<ref name="FPTP">DVD bonus disc of [[Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones|''Star Wars'': Episode II ''Attack of the Clones'']]: "From Puppets to Pixels"</ref>

In ''[[The Empire Strikes Back: So You Want to Be a Jedi?]]'', a [[canon]] retelling of [[Star Wars: Episode V The Empire Strikes Back|''Star Wars'': Episode V ''The Empire Strikes Back'']] written by [[Adam Gidwitz]], Luke Skywalker calls Yoda a "little swamp frog."<ref name="wannabe">''[[The Empire Strikes Back: So You Want to Be a Jedi?]]''</ref> In the [[2019]] canon audio drama ''[[Dooku: Jedi Lost]]'', the young [[noble]] [[Ramil]] claims that Yoda looked like a [[slime-gnome]].<ref name="DJL" />

[[Maz Kanata]], one of the main characters of the ''Star Wars'' [[sequel trilogy]], was originally sketched by [[Industrial Light & Magic]] concept artist [[Christian Alzmann]] as a member of Yoda's species around [[March]] [[2013]]. [[May|Three months later]], Alzmann redesigned the character as hunched, green alien with a headdress and, [[June|one month later]], redesigned her face to be bug-eyed and snub-nosed, distancing her from Yoda's design.<ref name="Art">''[[The Art of Star Wars: The Force Awakens]]''</ref>

